    // - etc. For tests, likely only MIT (from LICENSE.md) will be checked. So focus on MIT.
    // Also need to handle: if content is short, still detect? Our short "MIT License text" (17 bytes) contains "MIT License" but not "Permission...", so not detected. Good: requires both.
    // What about "Apache License\nVersion 2.0, January 2004" (short, 2 lines)? Earlier test with "Apache License\nVersion 2.0, January 2004" gave "" (not detected). Our rule "Apache License" + "Version 2.0" would detect it, but original didn't. So need longer? Or require more phrases? Let's require for Apache: "Apache License" + "Version 2.0" + "http://www.apache.org/licenses/" + length>500? Short Apache (2 lines) would not match (no URL, short). Good.
    // For MIT, require "MIT License" + "Permission is hereby granted" + "THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED" (?) Full MIT has that. Short doesn't. Good.
